<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17492" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fābŭlātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				narrator</i>, <i>a story-teller</i> (post-Aug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">elegantissimus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 122 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lectoribus aut fabulatoribus arcessitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 78</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Gell. 3, 10, 11</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vulg. Baruch, 3,
			23</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A fabulist</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesopus ille e Phrygia fabulator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					2, 29, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
